==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|ru|orv|берегъ}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*bergъ}}. {{doublet|ru|брег}}, a borrowing from Old Church Slavonic.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ru|бе́регъ||ru-PRO}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ru-IPA|бе́рег}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-берег.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|c|бе́рег|(1)|loc=на +|nom_pl_tail=*|acc_pl_tail=*|notes=* The irregular plural {{lang|ru|берега́}} is actually an old dual form, since rivers have two of them.|adj=берегово́й|dim=бережо́к}}

# [[bank]], [[shore]], [[coast]], [[beach]]
#: {{syn|ru|брег<q:poetic>}}
#* {{quote-book|ru|year=1859|author=w:ru:Иван Тургенев<t:{{w|Ivan Turgenev}}>|title=w:ru:Дворянское гнездо|chapter=s:ru:[[Дворянское гнездо (Тургенев)/Глава 26|Глава 26]]|location=|publisher=|newversion=English translation from|translator2=w:en:Constance Garnett|title2=s:en:[[A House of Gentlefolk/Chapter XXVI|A House of Gentlefolk]]|location2=|publisher2=|year2=1917|page2=|pageurl2=|text=Ма́рью Дми́триевну посади́ли на кре́сло во́зле '''бе́рега''', в тени́, постла́ли ей ковёр под но́ги, да́ли лу́чшую у́дочку[...]|t=Marya Dmitrievna was put in an arm-chair near the '''banks''', in the shade, with a rug under her feet and the best line was given to her.}}
#* {{quote-song|ru|year=2018|author={{w|lang=ru|Soft Blade}}|title=ru:Zerkalo|album=|text=Посмотри́, како́е холо́дное не́бо.<br>Э́тот '''бе́рег''' мне совсе́м незнако́м.|t=Look, how cold is the sky.<br>I don't know this '''shore''' at all|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=w-8zMhgrcuY}}
# [[land]]

=====Usage notes=====
* The stress may fall on the preposition in the expression {{m|ru|[[на́]] [[берег]]||[[ashore]]}}.

